    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d332">

                <pb facs="0426" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/3850</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mooney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Asuncion</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-14T17:00:00-03:50">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 14, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 15, 5.30 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Paraguayan Minister for Foreign Affairs, in reply to my advice of a state of
                    war between the United States and Germany, says in part as follows: “It is my
                    duty to make known to you that Paraguay and its Government in these moments
                    accompanies the United States and its Government with the most lively
                    sympathy.”</p>
                <p>Copy of reply by mail accompanied by translation.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d332-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mooney</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
